247 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (A 785 nm laser illuminates the material. Light that undergoes Rayleigh scattering is rejected using an edge/long-pass filter. A portion undergoes Raman scattering, producing wavelength shifts that correspond to the material's molecular vibrations.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (The Raman-shifted light is collected by the optics and passed through the spectrometer, which converts it into a Raman spectrum. The Raspberry Pi then performs dark correction, baseline correction, noise reduction and feature extraction, and compares the spectrum with the reference spectral library using PCA + ML analysis.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
